## Page 0114 / printed 107

The first two printed lines close inherited p0113#8 with the polynomial sum and the nested quotient:

`(b^(n-1)*(b/a)-a^(n-1))/(b/a-1) = ((b^n-a^n)/a)/((b-a)/a) = (b^n-a^n)/(b-a)`.

Both numerator/denominator order and all exponents match the new grid; there is no exchanged a/b or missing division level. The next block reverses both signs to `(a^n-b^n)/(a-b)`. Formula (1) retains the full n-term factor multiplied by `(a-b)` and its second physical line `=a^n-b^n`. Formula tags (1), (2), (3), and (4) are preserved once.

The assumptions `a != 0`, `b != 0`, `a != b`, and the printed sentence mentioning `a=b=0` are faithfully retained, without silently rewriting the source's explanatory argument. The n=2 difference-of-squares and n=3 difference-of-cubes specializations have the correct source signs. The example is exactly `8x^3-125y^3=(2x)^3-(5y)^3=(2x-5y)(4x^2+10xy+25y^2)`. Substitution of `-b` and formula (4), `(a+b)(a^2-ab+b^2)=a^3+b^3`, are complete.

